45	 * GAME_MOD_SYNC handler — reconcile a game server's installed mods to the desired
46	 * state recorded in `ServerMod` rows:
47	 *   - status INSTALLING → fetch + install the mod, then INSTALLED (or FAILED)
48	 *   - status REMOVING   → remove the mod, then delete the row (or FAILED)
49	 *
50	 * Wire into worker/index.ts handlers:  GAME_MOD_SYNC: gameModSync,
51	 *
52	 * ENGINE FAMILIES (2026-10-01 — minecraft, valheim, rust, cs2, factorio; see
53	 * lib/mods/installers/index.ts) go through lib/mods/engine.ts: verified
54	 * download, dependency resolution, safe placement, guest state file, rollback,
55	 * plus UPDATING / DISABLING / ENABLING. In SANDBOX they run the SAME pipeline
56	 * against a fake guest directory (lib/mods/guest-fs.ts LocalGuestFs) — real
57	 * downloads, real files, no simulated success.
58	 *
59	 * Every other family keeps the THREE PATHS below, mirroring game-config's
60	 * honesty guard so we never tell a customer a mod is installed when nothing
61	 * was written to their server:
62	 *  - SANDBOX: simulate (flip INSTALLING→INSTALLED, REMOVING→REMOVED). Dev only.
63	 *  - REAL (ENABLE_REAL_GAMEMODS=1, not sandbox): install/remove over SSH via the
64	 *    per-source adapter. Where an adapter isn't implemented yet, the mod is marked
65	 *    FAILED with a clear reason — never silently "INSTALLED".
66	 *  - Neither (production, flag off): mark the queued changes FAILED with a plain
67	 *    message. A change we did NOT apply is a failure and must say so.
68	 */
